// D-359 (landing 124): AN IMPL NAMES AT LEAST ONE TYPE OR TRAIT DECLARED IN ITS OWN MANIFEST'S TREE. An
// impl whose target names no type of this tree (a builtin, the prelude's, a generic parameter) and whose
// trait is not this tree's is NITPICK-TYPE-099 at the impl, once -- two libraries could each write it and
// collide under coherence in the program importing both (S-37's `impl:bool:Ord`, admitted until this
// landing). A type ARGUMENT counts (`List<Pt>` names `Pt`); an inherent impl's target must be the tree's
// own; a blanket impl's trait must be. A refused impl is the one report: no TYPE-013 against the prelude's
// row, no TYPE-087 for `Copy` on an owning type, no completeness question.

trait:Own = { func:own = int32(Self:self) never fails; };
